## Overview

Tidepool photo gallery — static site (index.html + app.js + zip.js), Android TWA dogfood app for the builds and deployments product plan.

## Goals

- Serve the gallery as a fast static site with client-side zip download.
- Ship the same experience as an Android TWA through the Play internal-testing lane.
- Dogfood the Surfspace builds and deployments pipeline end to end.

:::

::

The title is SurfDisplay-Black with edit-in-place; the body is the rendered SurfDoc. The meta line leads with the display-cased subtype label (Web / Doc / Presentation, else the capitalized slug — W-2), matching the docs-list row meta vocabulary.

**Website window frame (W-1, ruling R-1).** Website-type docs render their body inside a browser-window frame: a wrapper section (`bg=web-window` → `section-web-window`) styled as a rounded window with a neutral 1px border and a subtle 36px chrome header strip carrying three neutral window dots — no iframe, no accent border. The frame is CSS containment plus a transform: the transform makes the wrapper the containing block for the doc's own `position: fixed` chrome (nav bar, nav drawer), so that chrome pins inside the frame instead of the page viewport; `contain: layout paint` and `overflow: hidden` keep layout and paint inside. Frame anatomy lives surf-side in the live override layer (next-shell.css) and the body wrap in `splice_detail_pane`'s caller — no surf-parse change (ruling R-2). Presentation-type docs stay unframed (ruling R-4: not trivially free). Edit (from the ⋯ menu) swaps the main pane to `doc-editor`. Detail-bar actions are icon-only (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11): Ask Surfy rides the fin glyph, Share the share glyph, ⋯ the more glyph — the old visible labels carry as `aria-label`, verbs unchanged.

## Sheets and menus — defined once, opened from here

- **⋯ menu** — `modals/doc-menu.surf`: the anchored dropdown-select at full production-web parity (12 Actions with Move to trash danger-last, the General access single-select whose active option renders accent-filled with a checkmark, AI → Generate with Surfy). Anchors to a detail-bar ⋯ (`openDocMenu`) — the button is PARKED (not rendered) until WS-2 wires the verb; a menu, not a modal.
- **Share** — `modals/share.surf` (`name=share`), via a detail-bar Share (`openShare`, PARKED until WS-2 wires it) and the menu's Share link.
- **Rename** — `modals/rename.surf` (`name=rename`), via the menu (`openRename`).
- **Version history** — `modals/version-history.surf` (`name=version-history`), via the menu (`openVersionHistory`). Every save is a version; restore forks forward — history is never destroyed.
- **Move / Copy to workspace** — `modals/move-copy.surf` (`name=move-copy`), one sheet, two entry actions (`openMoveToWorkspace` / `openCopyToWorkspace`) that swap its title.
